# AWS Auto Scaling Group with Application Load Balancer and Nginx

## 1. Project Overview

This project demonstrates how to deploy a scalable web server infrastructure on Amazon Web Services (AWS) using an EC2 Launch Template, an Auto Scaling Group (ASG), an Application Load Balancer (ALB), and Nginx.

The infrastructure was deployed in the **US East (N. Virginia) region (`us-east-1`)**. The Application Load Balancer distributes incoming HTTP traffic to an EC2 instance running Nginx. Auto Scaling is configured to maintain the required instance capacity and adjust capacity based on average CPU utilization.

## 2. Objectives

- Create an EC2 launch template using Amazon Linux 2023.
- Configure Nginx to install and start automatically.
- Create an Auto Scaling Group with minimum, desired, and maximum capacities.
- Configure CPU target tracking at 50%.
- Create an HTTP target group with health checks.
- Configure an internet-facing Application Load Balancer on port 80.
- Verify the Nginx welcome page through the load balancer DNS endpoint.

